G4864.def:
**συν-αγωγή**, -ῆς, ἡ
[in LXX chiefly for עֵדָה, also for קָהָל, etc. ;]
prop., a bringing together;
1. of things,
(a) **a gathering in of harvest**;
(b) a collection of money.
2. **Of persons, **
(a) **a collecting, assembling **(Polyb.);
(b) **an assembly **(MM, xxiv; Deiss., _LAE_, 101 ff.): [[Rev.2.9; 3.9|Rev.2:9 3:9]]; esp. of a Jewish religious assembly, **a synagogue**: [[Luk.12.11|Luk.12:11]], [[Act.9.2|Act.9:2]], al.; of a Christian assembly, [[Jas.2.2|Jas.2:2]] By meton., of the building in which the assembly is held, **a synagogue**: [[Mat.10.17|Mat.10:17]], [[Mrk.1.21|Mrk.1:21]], al. (cf. Cremer, see word ἐκκλησία)
_SYN._: ἐκκλησία (which see) (AS)
